  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB25110",
    "sub_id": "31357",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>學期成績計算項目及權重標準如下： 每次上課均需要準備個人報告，報告內容可以是最新的財金新聞、期刊雜誌文章、商業趨勢介紹等等。 最終學期成績按所有報告分數的加權平均計算。 Grading rules are as follows: Each class everyone needs to prepare a personal report. The content of the report can be the latest financial news, journal articles, business trend introduction, etc. It is expected that there will be at least 13 individual reports in this semester, and the final grades will be calculated as the weighted average of all report scores.</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>Grading rules are as follows: Each class everyone needs to prepare a personal report. The content of&nbsp;report can be the latest financial news, journal articles, business trend introduction, fency ideas introduction, etc. Everyone but the one who makes the presentation has to ask questions after listeing to the report and this also counts. It is expected that there will be at least 13 individual reports in this semester, and the final grades will be calculated as the weighted average of all report scores.</div>\n",
    "course_pol": "本門課程對於修課學生的上課態度有所規範，希望培養學生尊重課堂、尊重講者的態度，上課不遲到、不缺席、不做與課堂無關的事，都是對於課堂的基本尊重，希望有意願修課的同學要規範好自己，共同創造充滿學習氛圍的課堂。",
    "course_pol_en": "(1) Attend class on time. During class, do not engage in conversations or other behaviors that may disturb others.\n(2) Do not request leave without valid reasons. If you need to be absent, please follow the school’s procedures.\n(3) If you do not understand something, feel free to actively discuss it with your classmates.\n(4) Comply with all classroom rules.",
    "course_rem": "學生課堂應該勇於提問，從講者身上學習到更多的理論知識與實務經驗，展現出積極的一面，相信每個講者都樂於分享給具備學習熱忱的學生，讓課堂充滿學習的氛圍。",
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>期望學生在學習評量、班上互動和課程結束後能展示學術誠信，包括不抄襲、不作弊並遵守學校和課程的相關規範。違反學術誠信的學生將面臨學校和課程規定的相應處分，可能包括但不限於失去評分資格、學科警告或更嚴重的學校紀律處分。希望學生能遵守學術誠信，以確保教學品質與個人成長。</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Students are expected to demonstrate integrity in all assessments by following examination rules and course requirements, including those for laboratory or practicum sessions. Throughout the course, students must avoid dishonest behaviors such as plagiarism or data fabrication. After the course concludes, students should continue to respect academic ethics and refrain from using others&rsquo; work without authorization. Any violations of academic integrity may result in disciplinary action.<br />\n&nbsp;</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
